analysis:
The only changed region is SSDPrefixCache.evictOldestEntry (base lines 1770-1787; head 1772-1777 per the patch). Both units supplied here are BASE text, so the new body is visible only in the patch excerpt.

Base behavior: it took a bounded index.oldestEntries() snapshot. It walked the victims oldest-first through retireIndexedEntries. It returned 0 on an externalChange, skipped a valid-but-undeletable entry, and returned the first nonzero indexedBytesFreed, counting one eviction.

Head behavior: it delegates victim iteration to SSDOwnedEntryRetirement.evictOldest(index:), with a closure calling retireIndexedEntries([url]). The closure is unchanged: it still uses removalLock, hasSafeRoot, ownsEvictionRoot, the epoch-store check and external-removal reconciliation (base 1793-1802). It increments evictions when freed > 0. The implementation of evictOldest is not in the supplied evidence.

T-041 mitigation (b) relies on the box-wide LRU disk budget. Integration must confirm that evictOldest preserves the base semantics:
- bounded iteration, with no unbounded loop or lock re-entrancy against removalLock;
- skipping undeletable entries so the budget can still be met;
- stopping on externalChange;
- dropping invalid or missing entries without touching their pathnames;
- oldest-by-lastAccess ordering.

A divergence would weaken disk-budget/TTL enforcement, an availability and at-rest retention concern under T-041/A-001, rather than confidentiality, because HMAC naming and DBK3 crypto are untouched.

No other changes were found. The donation per-donation gate (base 883-888), the durable-run cap, sidecar handling, staging reservations and the read-path binding checks (1392-1397, 1636-1650) are unchanged per range_map_complete=true. No regression was identified from the visible evidence. The missing helper source is a coverage limit, not proof of safety.
